WEBVTT

00:26.609 --> 00:29.070
I know you said
you'd never pick up a gun again.

00:30.864 --> 00:32.115
So why'd you become an officer?

00:34.784 --> 00:36.119
Because I think that

00:36.953 --> 00:40.165
there are plenty of ways to protect people
without using firearms.

00:43.168 --> 00:44.252
Right.

00:46.087 --> 00:49.132
- Welcome.
- Sergeant, shall we head inside?

00:49.924 --> 00:51.384
- Come in. Come.
- Come.

00:52.886 --> 00:55.764
So this is Officer Seo Jae-hui,
Sergeant Ahn Ji-wan,

00:55.847 --> 00:56.848
and Inspector Oh Dae-han.

00:56.931 --> 00:57.766
Hello.

01:02.854 --> 01:04.981
Shit! You're killing my vibe!

01:05.065 --> 01:07.817
Who the hell are you, old man?

01:08.443 --> 01:10.987
What the hell does your dead daughter

01:12.363 --> 01:14.282
have to do with me or anyone in here?

01:14.866 --> 01:17.202
I just saw my daughter at the morgue.

01:18.453 --> 01:20.580
Do not even dare to insult
the memory of her.

01:20.663 --> 01:24.626
What the fuck? Look, can someone just get
this crazy old man out of my fucking face?

01:24.709 --> 01:28.588
So what are you gonna do, pops?
What do you want us to do about it?

01:29.089 --> 01:30.131
Did we kill her?

01:30.632 --> 01:32.217
Huh? No, I don't think we did.

01:32.300 --> 01:34.719
So fuck off while we go back to our party.

01:34.803 --> 01:37.013
What do you want from me? Huh?

01:37.806 --> 01:39.849
Apologize at my daughter's funeral.

01:40.767 --> 01:42.310
Apol… apologize?

01:42.393 --> 01:44.437
Shit. Is that what she asked for? Huh?

01:45.313 --> 01:48.024
Unless you wanna join your dead daughter
at the morgue,

01:48.733 --> 01:50.985
I'd suggest leaving now
before I really lose my temper.

01:51.069 --> 01:52.737
Just fuckin' forget about him.

01:52.821 --> 01:54.989
- Get outta here.
- Fucking buzzkill.

01:55.073 --> 01:56.741
- Get the fuck out!
- What's going on?

01:56.825 --> 01:59.077
I said, get the fuck out,
you stupid old shit!

02:01.371 --> 02:02.914
Oh my God!

02:10.046 --> 02:11.714
What the fuck are you doing?

02:11.798 --> 02:13.508
Fuck!

02:15.927 --> 02:17.554
Come here! Don't shoot!

02:17.637 --> 02:19.597
She just died,

02:21.057 --> 02:23.685
and you people don't feel
any guilt at all.

02:25.645 --> 02:27.522
How utterly hopeless is that?

02:29.858 --> 02:31.651
Please. Please don't kill me.

02:31.734 --> 02:33.778
Please, please.

02:33.862 --> 02:36.656
Don't… don't shoot me. I'll do anything.

02:36.739 --> 02:40.076
Sir, please help me. I need this money.

02:40.160 --> 02:42.453
Please, please. Please, sir, have mercy.

02:42.537 --> 02:45.665
I'm begging you, sir.
Oh please, please, please!

02:45.748 --> 02:47.584
Please will you help me?!

02:50.128 --> 02:51.462
Why didn't you help her?

02:54.299 --> 02:56.676
- Why didn't you spare my daughter?
- Please…

02:57.343 --> 02:59.220
You fucking piece of shit!

02:59.304 --> 03:02.557
Get off me! Get me out of here!

03:16.571 --> 03:18.156
Hey! Hey there! You gotta help me.

03:18.239 --> 03:20.074
- What is up with you?
- That guy has a gun!

03:20.158 --> 03:21.201
That crazy fucker!

03:21.284 --> 03:23.494
Look! He's over there! He's got a gun!

03:23.578 --> 03:24.787
Look, he's got a gun.

03:25.455 --> 03:27.540
That crazy old bastard has a gun!

03:42.430 --> 03:43.848
Oh fuck!

03:48.144 --> 03:49.646
Help me, please!

03:55.985 --> 03:57.278
Drop the gun!

03:59.364 --> 04:00.990
I said drop the gun!

04:08.289 --> 04:12.085
- H… help! Help me! Help me!
- Drop the gun!

04:13.169 --> 04:15.421
Oh, please! Help me! I'm begging!

04:20.176 --> 04:22.929
How exactly did you know there was
gonna be a shooting here, Wang?

04:23.513 --> 04:25.848
That's none of your concern.
Just get the shot.

04:30.937 --> 04:32.188
Hey, point it over there.

04:41.322 --> 04:42.740
Wait! Hold your fire!

04:45.702 --> 04:48.121
I'm Officer Lee Do
from Domyeong Precinct Station.

04:48.204 --> 04:50.039
Let me try to talk him down, okay?

04:54.877 --> 04:56.713
Lee Do.

04:59.257 --> 05:00.425
Sergeant, what…

05:02.093 --> 05:03.303
Don't come any closer.

05:13.771 --> 05:16.316
You know better than anyone else
that doing this

05:17.900 --> 05:19.777
still won't bring Se-yeong back.

05:28.036 --> 05:29.245
So drop the gun.

05:30.913 --> 05:33.499
You're right.
I did think I knew better than anyone.

05:38.921 --> 05:41.466
I believed that arresting
scumbags just like him,

05:41.549 --> 05:44.469
like you, over and over,
the entire lot of them…

05:46.846 --> 05:50.058
would somehow mean justice
for all the poor innocent victims.

05:52.560 --> 05:54.729
And that's exactly what you've done,
Sergeant.

06:00.151 --> 06:00.985
No.

06:02.111 --> 06:03.571
I had no idea…

06:06.240 --> 06:09.285
that I actually knew
absolutely nothing at all.

06:15.958 --> 06:17.877
Now my eyes are finally open.

06:18.544 --> 06:20.797
What the fuck are you all doing?

06:22.090 --> 06:25.635
Are you just gonna watch him
shoot me down like a dog?! Huh?!

06:32.433 --> 06:34.394
Don't shoot. Please don't shoot.

06:35.353 --> 06:37.688
This is the limitation of law enforcement.

06:39.107 --> 06:40.817
It basically doesn't exist now.

06:45.446 --> 06:46.614
I'm sorry.

06:47.657 --> 06:49.575
I've already made up my mind.

06:51.160 --> 06:52.578
Please, Sergeant, wait!

06:53.663 --> 06:55.790
Don't let yourself
be fooled by that feeling.

06:57.041 --> 06:59.168
Do you remember what you told me that day?

07:01.546 --> 07:02.755
When I held that gun?

07:03.506 --> 07:04.340
Lee Do!

07:07.593 --> 07:08.928
I promise,

07:09.011 --> 07:11.139
and so do all these grown-ups,

07:12.140 --> 07:15.643
I promise to make sure
to punish that bad guy.

07:16.352 --> 07:17.687
My mom

07:18.354 --> 07:19.730
and my dad

07:20.231 --> 07:22.567
and my brother, he murdered them all!

07:23.401 --> 07:26.779
But he's just eating bread
and smiling like nothing's wrong!

07:27.530 --> 07:29.490
He shouldn't be allowed to live!

07:29.574 --> 07:31.409
Yes, I know he's a murderer,

07:31.492 --> 07:34.287
and you're right to be angry, but think.

07:35.621 --> 07:37.623
If you shoot that gun right now, Do…

07:39.625 --> 07:43.463
then that will actually just make
that bastard's life easier, understand?

07:44.046 --> 07:45.882
Scumbags like this guy,

07:46.799 --> 07:49.594
they should all be sent right to prison
to pay for what they did

07:49.677 --> 07:50.928
for the rest of their lives.

07:51.679 --> 07:52.597
No.

07:54.515 --> 07:55.725
I really think

07:57.393 --> 07:59.228
I'll only feel better if I kill him.

07:59.979 --> 08:03.191
Don't let yourself be fooled
by that feeling, please! It passes.

08:03.774 --> 08:06.235
That feeling of satisfaction will fade.

08:08.112 --> 08:10.031
Except it's a good deed…

08:12.909 --> 08:14.785
if you kill a bad person.

08:19.081 --> 08:20.917
But then what about your future?

08:22.001 --> 08:23.211
If you kill that man,

08:24.378 --> 08:26.923
then you're going to ruin your whole life.

08:29.509 --> 08:31.761
So please just trust me. Just this once.

08:31.844 --> 08:33.471
I'll make you a promise.

08:34.096 --> 08:36.307
I promise to make you understand that…

08:36.390 --> 08:38.768
that not shooting him was the right thing.

08:38.851 --> 08:41.270
So what do you say? Hmm?

08:41.771 --> 08:44.273
Will you do it for me?
Will you put that gun down?

08:44.357 --> 08:45.650
Hmm? Will you, please?

08:49.111 --> 08:52.615
And in the end, all we were able to do
was send him to prison.

08:54.033 --> 08:55.535
And what does that matter?

08:58.538 --> 09:01.332
Thanks to you, Sergeant,
I didn't end up ruining my life.

09:03.459 --> 09:05.127
If something happens to you…

09:07.588 --> 09:09.090
how will I be able to go on?

09:10.591 --> 09:11.801
So tell me.

09:11.884 --> 09:14.554
Are you still not gonna take
the next promotion exam?

09:15.263 --> 09:17.765
I like my job.
I'm comfortable enough here.

09:17.848 --> 09:18.891
I mean, listen.

09:19.684 --> 09:22.520
Given your age, your talent,
your experience, and your skills,

09:22.603 --> 09:27.692
you know you should at the very least
be a sergeant by now, Lee Do.

09:30.152 --> 09:32.655
Where are all these guns even coming from?

09:32.738 --> 09:35.157
You worked so hard
to never have to hold a gun again.

09:40.746 --> 09:43.165
Just don't get involved
if you don't have to.

09:44.875 --> 09:47.211
I can't bear to see you get hurt again.

09:47.295 --> 09:49.589
Physically or mentally.

09:51.007 --> 09:52.216
I'm begging you.

09:54.218 --> 09:55.219
Sergeant,

09:56.887 --> 09:57.722
give me the gun.

10:13.613 --> 10:14.614
Lee Do.

10:18.200 --> 10:19.660
How were you able to…

10:21.120 --> 10:24.081
to endure this much pain
when you were just a boy?

10:28.961 --> 10:31.047
It was all because of you, Sergeant.

10:34.759 --> 10:36.052
Aw…

10:40.348 --> 10:42.642
Well, this isn't what I wanted.

11:09.835 --> 11:12.004
Hey! Come here.
Shoot here. Shoot from here.

11:18.302 --> 11:19.762
Hey, Lee Do!

11:30.731 --> 11:33.359
Lee Do!

12:30.708 --> 12:31.542
Lee Do…

12:37.298 --> 12:38.215
I'm sorr…

12:39.675 --> 12:40.634
Sergeant.

12:40.718 --> 12:42.386
Sergeant!

13:49.161 --> 13:50.204
You did well.

13:51.455 --> 13:52.456
You did so well.

13:58.003 --> 13:59.296
Stupid grown-ups.

14:02.341 --> 14:03.676
I'm so sorry, Lee Do.

14:21.777 --> 14:22.862
Let's go downstairs.

14:22.945 --> 14:23.946
What?

14:24.446 --> 14:26.490
I'm not going down there.
That guy's got a gun.

14:26.574 --> 14:29.201
You're such a fucking coward. Hey.

14:29.285 --> 14:30.411
Give me that camera.

14:54.435 --> 14:58.063
Can you even remember how many people
you've killed using a gun?

15:02.026 --> 15:05.446
I heard that you'd kill anyone at all
back when you were a mercenary.

15:07.907 --> 15:08.991
Except that now

15:10.284 --> 15:11.911
you only kill some people,

15:12.912 --> 15:14.413
and you save others.

15:18.584 --> 15:20.628
Is that what you think justice is?

15:22.838 --> 15:25.215
All of this is your fault.

15:26.175 --> 15:27.885
For being a hypocrite.

15:34.141 --> 15:35.267
You disgust me,

15:36.852 --> 15:37.770
Lee Do.

15:46.111 --> 15:47.154
Although…

15:49.490 --> 15:51.492
…I guess you were pretty entertaining
at least.

15:58.540 --> 15:59.500
Just wait.

16:01.627 --> 16:03.921
You're gonna wake up to a whole new world.

16:19.895 --> 16:21.647
- You get all that?
- Yeah.

16:21.730 --> 16:23.774
I'm getting some great footage.

16:25.109 --> 16:28.278
Hello. My name is Moon Baek,
and I am behind

16:29.446 --> 16:31.699
all of the shootings. I'm the mastermind.

16:34.660 --> 16:35.494
As you can see,

16:35.577 --> 16:38.747
South Korea is no longer immune
to the threat of firearms.

16:39.248 --> 16:41.417
- So I've prepared…
- What's that?

16:42.042 --> 16:43.460
- …a little gift for you all.
- Look.

16:44.044 --> 16:45.337
Starting right now,

16:46.005 --> 16:50.426
regardless of your age,
gender, occupation,

16:50.926 --> 16:53.595
or your nationality,
if you would like a gun,

16:54.430 --> 16:57.975
then I am prepared to give it to you
with no strings attached.

17:02.521 --> 17:03.647
I repeat.

17:04.148 --> 17:07.943
Starting right now,
regardless of your age, gender,

17:08.527 --> 17:10.779
occupation, or your nationality…

17:14.241 --> 17:15.242
…if you would like a gun,

17:15.325 --> 17:17.911
I will give it to you
with no strings attached.

17:18.954 --> 17:20.748
I don't wanna force anyone.

17:20.831 --> 17:24.376
I just wanna give you
the power to protect yourselves.

17:24.460 --> 17:26.670
You're the manager,
so why don't you manage this place?

17:28.881 --> 17:31.592
Moon Baek. Moon Baek.

17:44.354 --> 17:45.773
Hey! Hold onto him.

17:45.856 --> 17:49.068
His pulse is dropping.
We need to get the bleeding under control.

17:49.151 --> 17:52.071
- Compression bandage and gauze, please.
- Here you go.

18:01.914 --> 18:03.457
Move! We're in a rush here!

18:05.709 --> 18:06.710
Bed number four.

18:08.045 --> 18:10.631
On three. One, two, three!

18:12.257 --> 18:14.426
- A gunshot victim?
- Yes, he was shot.

18:14.510 --> 18:16.678
Check his vitals.
Prepare him for a transfusion.

18:16.762 --> 18:17.679
Yes, Doctor!

18:17.763 --> 18:20.599
Get ready.

18:22.643 --> 18:25.020
You're gonna wake up to a whole new world.

18:55.259 --> 18:56.301
GYEONGIN EXPRESS

19:14.153 --> 19:15.863
Wow! I finally got my gun in the mail.

19:15.946 --> 19:19.032
South Korea's in a new era
where you can order a gun to your house!

19:19.116 --> 19:20.701
This footage was captured

19:20.784 --> 19:22.995
as someone live-streamed
a police officer on active duty

19:23.078 --> 19:25.372
being shot by the organization
behind all these guns.

19:25.455 --> 19:28.625
Today, I wanna get the Super Chat
up to 30 million won this time, all right?

19:28.709 --> 19:30.043
Woo-hoo!

19:30.127 --> 19:34.464
It is my sincerest hope
that Officer Lee can pull through

19:35.090 --> 19:36.341
and wake up as soon as possible.

19:43.473 --> 19:46.310
Unmarked packages
containing firearms and ammunition

19:46.393 --> 19:48.478
are being shipped all over the country.

19:49.188 --> 19:51.773
Authorities are on high alert
for the potential risk,

19:51.857 --> 19:53.859
thanks to guns
being delivered by courier services,

19:53.942 --> 19:55.402
of another deadly shooting incident.

19:55.485 --> 19:58.071
Even declaring martial law
wouldn't be enough in this situation.

19:58.155 --> 20:00.115
No. I don't think we're there yet.

20:00.199 --> 20:02.326
Haven't you seen
what's going on out there?

20:02.409 --> 20:04.703
The priority is to get
an accurate sense of the situation.

20:04.786 --> 20:07.831
Given that the crime was committed
under the influence of alcohol,

20:07.915 --> 20:10.751
that it was a first offense,
and the defendant has shown remorse,

20:10.834 --> 20:13.503
I hereby sentence the defendant
to three years in prison with a--

20:13.587 --> 20:14.755
I object!

20:14.838 --> 20:15.797
Excuse me?

20:15.881 --> 20:18.258
Since you won't be executing him today,

20:18.342 --> 20:20.427
I decided to simply do it myself.

20:24.014 --> 20:25.807
Whoa! How amazing was that, huh?

20:25.891 --> 20:27.601
I don't think
you need a real gun with these.

20:27.684 --> 20:29.519
Look at this. Looks like a real gun, huh?

20:29.603 --> 20:32.773
And, with the right modifications,
air guns can be deadlier than real ones.

20:32.856 --> 20:35.150
Random distribution of guns is instilling

20:35.234 --> 20:39.529
a growing fear among citizens
that anyone around them might have one.

20:39.613 --> 20:43.450
As a result, people are lining up
in droves, rushing to buy guns.

20:43.533 --> 20:47.287
Here's a gun from the good old days,
an M16, and it's only 20,000 won.

20:47.371 --> 20:49.665
- I'll take one!
- I'll take one!

20:49.748 --> 20:52.167
- How much do you want for it?
- Okay, well, don't worry.

20:52.251 --> 20:53.710
I've got another bunch of pistols.

20:53.794 --> 20:55.128
So, until now,

20:55.212 --> 20:58.632
sociopathic tendencies
had been fairly repressed and contained.

20:58.715 --> 21:01.343
These guns are triggering
those suppressed emotions.

21:02.135 --> 21:03.262
But the real problem

21:03.345 --> 21:05.264
is that these anxious feelings

21:05.931 --> 21:08.016
are much more contagious
than you might think.

21:08.100 --> 21:10.811
I thought I told you to submit
the report before you went home.

21:10.894 --> 21:13.855
Right, sir. But I've been working nights
for three weeks.

21:14.773 --> 21:17.526
- It's also my daughter's birthday today.
- You useless moron.

21:17.609 --> 21:19.278
You think
you're the only one with a family?

21:19.361 --> 21:21.446
Why don't you just quit
if you have a problem working?

21:21.530 --> 21:22.572
I understand, sir.

21:23.156 --> 21:26.410
I'll just watch her blow out the candles,
and then I'll head back to work.

21:27.452 --> 21:29.663
Fuck, I wish I could put a bullet
in that guy's head.

21:37.337 --> 21:39.256
Welcome home.

21:39.339 --> 21:40.799
- Daddy!
- Hmm?

21:40.882 --> 21:42.926
This looks like a real gun!

21:47.889 --> 21:49.308
GYEONGIN UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

22:01.820 --> 22:03.739
Panic is seizing the country.

22:03.822 --> 22:06.408
Many people are refusing
to leave their homes,

22:06.908 --> 22:09.953
and busy thoroughfares have become
practically deserted as a result.

22:12.956 --> 22:14.249
Yes, Mr. President.

22:17.002 --> 22:17.919
Yes.

22:18.420 --> 22:20.005
I'll relay the message, sir.

22:26.345 --> 22:28.847
We're declaring
a national state of emergency.

22:30.349 --> 22:31.975
I don't think there's ever been

22:32.059 --> 22:33.894
a time of greater conflict than now.

22:34.394 --> 22:36.980
Remember the early days of COVID-19?

22:37.064 --> 22:39.858
Masks sold out nationwide
in just three days.

22:39.941 --> 22:42.569
So tell me. Who would just sit back,

22:42.652 --> 22:44.905
watching while guns spread
through the nation?

22:44.988 --> 22:49.451
While the two of you were in conversation,
shocking poll results were just released.

22:49.534 --> 22:53.789
Over 40% think that gun ownership
should be legal in Korea.

22:53.872 --> 22:55.957
And as for the question
of conditional permission,

22:56.041 --> 22:58.460
over half of the participants
were in favor.

22:58.543 --> 23:01.088
NUMBER OF PACKAGES IN TRANSIT
NUMBER OF PACKAGES RETRIEVED

23:01.171 --> 23:03.507
The amount of packages we've collected
is too low.

23:03.590 --> 23:05.926
There are four million packages
in circulation every day.

23:06.009 --> 23:08.553
There's no way we can keep up with it.

23:08.637 --> 23:10.847
South Korea was once drug-free,

23:10.931 --> 23:13.517
and now it's a country
where people who want drugs

23:13.600 --> 23:17.187
can simply get their hands on them
wherever or whenever they want.

23:17.270 --> 23:19.898
How… are guns any different?

23:19.981 --> 23:24.277
Right. The appearance of more
and more guns of unknown origin

23:24.361 --> 23:26.822
is heralding major changes in our society.

23:26.905 --> 23:30.659
We want to know your opinion
on the issue of legalizing gun ownership.

23:30.742 --> 23:32.869
Good morning. Please sign our petition.

23:32.953 --> 23:35.414
Hello there, sir!
Would you like to sign our petition?

23:35.497 --> 23:36.873
Okay, thanks.

23:36.957 --> 23:38.625
We are strongly opposed
to legalizing guns!

23:38.708 --> 23:41.837
Strongly opposed? Come on, man!
Even when we didn't have guns,

23:41.920 --> 23:44.840
people were attacking each other
with knives in broad daylight here.

23:44.923 --> 23:46.716
Now those lunatics are going to show up

23:46.800 --> 23:48.718
in schools and daycares
and hospitals with guns.

23:48.802 --> 23:52.055
By that logic, then even teachers
and doctors should be carrying guns.

23:52.139 --> 23:54.099
- You see how messed up this is?
- Exactly!

23:54.182 --> 23:55.684
You don't care! People like you,

23:55.767 --> 23:58.395
encouraging people to shoot places up
in the middle of the day,

23:58.478 --> 23:59.479
should be put in jail.

23:59.563 --> 24:01.773
Our kids could end up
being caught in the crossfire!

24:01.857 --> 24:04.025
That's exactly why we need guns.
To protect the children.

24:04.109 --> 24:04.943
Exactly!

24:05.026 --> 24:08.947
If every one of us had a gun,
no one would show up anywhere with a gun.

24:09.030 --> 24:11.533
- Now you're being ridiculous!
- Are you hearing what you're saying?

24:11.616 --> 24:13.785
Hey, you asshole!
What do you think you're doing?!

24:15.662 --> 24:18.623
The empty streets are
slowly filling up with protestors.

24:18.707 --> 24:22.544
Widespread public fear of guns
is leading to more and more unrest,

24:22.627 --> 24:24.921
with disagreements between protestors
progressing rapidly…

24:25.005 --> 24:28.216
All the shipped items
were delivered without incident.

24:28.300 --> 24:30.510
The public is divided
into two distinct camps…

24:30.594 --> 24:31.803
Time for the next step.

24:33.054 --> 24:34.014
Get ready.

24:40.103 --> 24:42.189
How are you, sir? Feeling any discomfort?

24:42.272 --> 24:43.607
No, I'm fine.

24:51.948 --> 24:53.825
I'll see you
for your afternoon check-up later.

24:53.909 --> 24:54.826
Okay.

24:59.831 --> 25:01.291
You're not busy at night, right?

25:01.374 --> 25:03.376
Next week,
the head nurse is evaluating us,

25:03.460 --> 25:05.378
which means
you need to get all that done today.

25:05.462 --> 25:06.963
We don't want any team issues.

25:07.756 --> 25:08.673
Oh…

25:08.757 --> 25:10.842
No. I won't have time to do this.

25:11.551 --> 25:13.053
I'm working tonight too.

25:13.595 --> 25:14.763
Too bad for you.

25:15.514 --> 25:17.682
You're talking back to me now, huh?

25:17.766 --> 25:19.643
There are hardly any forms here.

25:19.726 --> 25:21.978
It just seems hard
because you're too stupid.

25:23.355 --> 25:24.523
All right, I'll do it.

26:01.059 --> 26:02.602
Usually, we're at each other's throats,

26:02.686 --> 26:05.438
so why the hell are we seeing each other
so often now?

26:06.565 --> 26:08.149
It's starting to feel like we're married.

26:08.233 --> 26:11.528
Please. You came here
for the exact same reasons that we did.

26:11.611 --> 26:14.155
So why don't you just keep
that big mouth of yours shut?

26:15.824 --> 26:17.742
The world is changing so fast.

26:18.618 --> 26:21.246
Should we stay still?
We all need to change

26:21.329 --> 26:24.249
so we don't get shot and killed
like Mr. Gong.

26:24.332 --> 26:26.418
- What is this, a funeral?
- What?

26:27.419 --> 26:30.714
You all look so sad.
Didn't you all come here to get guns?

26:30.797 --> 26:31.798
If not, I'll go.

26:32.382 --> 26:35.051
Is he joking?
He can't talk to us like that.

26:35.135 --> 26:39.347
Hey! Who do you think you are, you punk?
Huh?

26:39.431 --> 26:42.058
Think you can just walk in here
like you own the place?

26:46.271 --> 26:49.274
Why is it that age equals respect?

26:49.983 --> 26:51.818
Are you all really that surprised?

26:52.652 --> 26:54.446
I mean, you've seen people die.

26:55.196 --> 26:57.073
All right. Get one last good look,

26:57.157 --> 26:59.242
because now we're gonna focus
and get serious.

26:59.326 --> 27:00.660
I'm looking for a new partner.

27:00.744 --> 27:03.038
But too many cooks spoil the broth, right?

27:03.121 --> 27:06.541
The thing is that now I'm just looking for
one very special person.

27:11.296 --> 27:13.131
Whoever shoots me with that gun.

27:13.632 --> 27:14.507
One person.

27:14.591 --> 27:15.634
Come on.

27:20.096 --> 27:22.432
You fuckers! Everybody back off!

27:26.811 --> 27:28.647
This should be easier than a knife.

27:31.107 --> 27:32.108
Go on.

27:32.192 --> 27:35.028
Do we look stupid?
You think we're fucking idiots?

27:35.111 --> 27:37.864
What? You think I won't shoot you,
you fucking asshole?

27:37.947 --> 27:40.200
- Come on. Shoot me.
- You fucking piece of shit.

27:40.283 --> 27:41.493
You goddamn motherfucker!

27:42.577 --> 27:43.745
Oh…

27:44.412 --> 27:45.789
Huh?

27:54.005 --> 27:55.840
Hmm…

28:18.905 --> 28:20.740
You scared?

28:25.286 --> 28:26.621
Make sure to pick up my calls.

28:29.916 --> 28:31.501
And get this place cleaned up.

28:41.302 --> 28:43.138
GYEONGIN UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

29:02.574 --> 29:05.452
As of yesterday,
your body count was up to 99.

29:05.535 --> 29:07.996
After today, it's 100 people.

29:08.079 --> 29:12.000
Truth is,
you wanted to kill them all, didn't you?

29:15.336 --> 29:17.255
At 27 Baekju-ro,

29:17.338 --> 29:20.425
there's someone
who's about to pull a trigger right now.

29:20.508 --> 29:22.218
Lee Do!

29:55.418 --> 29:56.252
You've woken up.

29:58.880 --> 30:00.423
Oh! No, don't move.

30:00.507 --> 30:02.050
You need to rest for now.

30:03.301 --> 30:04.469
Where's Sergeant Jo?

30:04.969 --> 30:05.970
Sir.

30:06.930 --> 30:08.556
Sir, please calm down.

30:08.640 --> 30:09.766
No! Sir!

30:10.350 --> 30:12.477
- You shouldn't stand up too quickly.
- Sergeant Jo.

30:13.228 --> 30:15.146
- We've got to find Sergeant Jo.
- Sir, wait.

30:15.230 --> 30:17.148
- Please!
- His name is Jo Hyeon-sik.

30:17.232 --> 30:18.566
Sir, be careful.

30:18.650 --> 30:19.901
- Sir, please!
- Hey.

30:19.984 --> 30:21.486
Oh!

30:21.569 --> 30:23.822
Oh God, are you all right?

30:23.905 --> 30:25.490
- What happened to Sergeant Jo?
- Please.

30:25.573 --> 30:27.784
Careful! Sir, you have to calm down.

30:27.867 --> 30:29.285
Which room is Jo Hyeon-sik in?

30:29.369 --> 30:30.954
Excuse me, h… have you seen…

30:31.037 --> 30:33.039
- I want to help.
- Has anybody seen Jo Hyeon-sik?

30:33.122 --> 30:36.125
H-he is a sergeant at our precinct.
Can you tell me where he is?

30:36.209 --> 30:38.336
- I…
- Officer Lee.
